 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3l-2.5-3z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"13\" r=\"3\"/></svg><span>Enter Photobooth</span></a><a href=\"/studio\" class=\"drawer-cta-secondary\" aria-label=\"Explore Studio\"><svg class=\"cta-grid-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:18px;height:18px;vertical-align:-.15em;display:inline-block;flex-shrink:0\"><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"14\" y=\"3\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"14\" y=\"14\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"3\" y=\"14\" rx=\"1\"/></svg><span>Explore Studio</span></a></div><div class=\"mobile-menu-footer\"><span class=\"mobile-menu-footer-brand\">ConstBooth<br><span style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:normal\">One frame. Beyond distance.</span></span><span class=\"mobile-menu-footer-version\">v2.0.0</span></div></nav><header class=\"main-header full-header\"><div class=\"header-left\"><a href=\"/\" id=\"logo-trigger-top\" class=\"app-logo\" aria-label=\"ConstBooth\"><img src=\"/assets/logo.svg?v=35ddb567\" alt=\"ConstBooth\" class=\"logo-img\" width=\"134\" height=\"36\"></a></div><nav class=\"header-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/#booth-types\">Booths</a> <a href=\"/studio\">Studio</a> <a href=\"/#how\">How it works</a> <a href=\"/blog\">Blog</a> <a href=\"/contact\">Contact</a></nav><div class=\"header-actions\"><a href=\"/booth\" class=\"nav-cta\"><svg class=\"cta-icon-camera\" aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:1.18em;height:1.18em;vertical-align:-.18em;margin-right:7px;display:inline-block;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M14.5 4h-5L7 7H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3l-2.5-3z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"13\" r=\"3\"/></svg><span>Enter Photobooth</span></a></div></header><main id=\"main-content\"><div class=\"blog-page-wrap\"><div class=\"blog-container\"></div><section class=\"blog-hero\"><nav class=\"blog-eyebrow reveal\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\" class=\"blog-eyebrow-link\">Home</a><span class=\"blog-crumb-sep\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&middot;</span><a href=\"/blog\" class=\"blog-eyebrow-link\">Blog</a><span class=\"blog-crumb-sep\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&middot;</span><a href=\"/blog/category/studio\" class=\"blog-eyebrow-link\">Studio</a></nav><h1 class=\"reveal delay-1\">How to Make a <span class=\"accent\">Digital Love Letter</span> Online With Photos & Memories</h1><p class=\"blog-hero-sub reveal delay-2\">A text says what happened. A letter says you thought about how to say it - here's how to write, fold and send one online.</p><div class=\"blog-meta reveal delay-3\"><div class=\"blog-meta-author\"><div class=\"blog-meta-avatar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7\" r=\"4\"/></svg></div><span class=\"blog-meta-name\"><a href=\"/about#author\">Kishan Naik</a></span></div><span class=\"blog-meta-date\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:14px;height:14px;opacity:.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> <time datetime=\"2026-09-18\">September 18, 2026</time> </span><span class=\"blog-meta-read\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:14px;height:14px;opacity:.5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 7 min read</span></div></section><div class=\"blog-container\"><aside class=\"lb-rail lb-rail--blog lb-rail--follow lb-rail--l\" data-rail=\"blog\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><div class=\"lb-rail-ad\"></div></aside><aside class=\"lb-rail lb-rail--blog lb-rail--follow lb-rail--r\" data-rail=\"blog\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><div class=\"lb-rail-ad\"></div></aside>\n<figure class=\"blog-cover reveal\"><picture><source type=\"image/avif\" srcset=\"/assets/blog/digital-love-letter-online-960.avif?v=e2961c1d 960w, /assets/blog/digital-love-letter-online-1920.avif?v=cce69dfd 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/assets/blog/digital-love-letter-online-960.webp?v=a70436c1 960w, /assets/blog/digital-love-letter-online-1920.webp?v=c3f3b6b7 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px\"><img src=\"/assets/blog/digital-love-letter-online-960.webp?v=a70436c1\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"A handwritten digital letter with a photo strip, beside a kraft paper envelope\" loading=\"eager\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\"></picture></figure><article class=\"blog-body\" id=\"blog-article\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/BlogPosting\"><nav class=\"blog-toc reveal\" aria-labelledby=\"toc-heading\"><h2 id=\"toc-heading\" class=\"blog-toc-title\">In this article</h2><ol class=\"blog-toc-list\"><li><a href=\"#s1\">What is a digital love letter?</a></li><li><a href=\"#s2\">What to put in a digital love letter</a></li><li><a href=\"#s3\">How to create one in ConstBooth</a></li><li><a href=\"#s4\">Digital love letter ideas</a></li><li><a href=\"#s5\">Digital letter vs. a normal message</a></li><li><a href=\"#s6\">If you'd rather record than write</a></li><li><a href=\"#faq\">Frequently Asked Questions</a></li></ol></nav>\n<section class=\"blog-section\"><p class=\"reveal\">A text says what happened. A letter says you thought about how to say it. That difference is the entire case for a digital love letter: not that it looks nicer than a message, but that writing one takes long enough to force you to actually think about what you're saying.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">ConstBooth Letters is a realistic digital paper letter you write directly on the page, attach photos to, fold, and put into an envelope before sending. This is what it's for, what to put in one, and how to make one.</p></section>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s1\"><h2 id=\"s1\" class=\"reveal\">What is a digital love letter?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">It's a letter that keeps the physical gestures of a real one - writing on a page, folding it, sealing it in an envelope - but is made and sent online. The point isn't to imitate paper for its own sake. It's that those gestures are what make a letter feel like an event rather than a message: you sit down, you write, you fold it closed, and only then does it go anywhere.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A digital love letter isn't only for couples, despite the name. The same format works for a friend who moved away, a parent, a thank-you note that deserves more than a text - anywhere a normal message would feel too quick for what you're actually trying to say.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">It also solves a specific problem a normal message can't: a photo strip or photo on its own has no context once it's a week old, and a message on its own has no image to anchor it. A letter puts both on the same page, so the photo explains the words and the words explain the photo. Neither one needs a caption doing all the work.</p></section>\n\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s2\"><h2 id=\"s2\" class=\"reveal\">What to put in a digital love letter</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A blank page is the hardest part of any letter. A few things worth including, in whatever combination fits:</p><ul class=\"blog-list reveal delay-1\"><li><strong>The actual message.</strong> Obvious, but it's worth deciding first whether this is a letter about a specific thing (a trip, an anniversary, an apology) or a general one, because that changes how you open it.</li><li><strong>A favorite photo, or a photo strip.</strong> A single image tied to the letter's subject does more work than a paragraph describing it.</li><li><strong>A meaningful date.</strong> When you met, when something happened, or just today's date written the way you'd write it by hand.</li><li><strong>A location.</strong> Where you are, where they are, or where the memory took place.</li><li><strong>Small decorations or stickers.</strong> Not required, but they're what stop a letter looking like a printed document.</li><li><strong>An inside joke or specific memory.</strong> The single most effective way to make a letter feel like it could only have been written to one person.</li></ul></section>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s3\"><h2 id=\"s3\" class=\"reveal\">How to create one in ConstBooth</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">The actual process, start to finish:</p><ol class=\"blog-list reveal delay-1\"><li><strong>Open Letters in Studio.</strong> Go to <a href=\"/studio/letters\" class=\"inline-link\">ConstBooth Letters</a> to start.</li><li><strong>Start a letter.</strong> You'll land on a blank page ready to write on.</li><li><strong>Write your message.</strong> Type directly onto the paper.</li><li><strong>Add photos or photo strips.</strong> Upload an existing photo, or attach a photo strip you've already made in ConstBooth.</li><li><strong>Adjust what you've added.</strong> Resize and reposition the supported elements - photo, date, location, decorations - until the page looks right.</li><li><strong>Fold the letter.</strong> Once you're happy with it, fold it the way you would a physical letter.</li><li><strong>Place it in the envelope and send.</strong> Share it using one of the supported outputs, or save it.</li></ol><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">The whole thing takes a few minutes. Nothing about it requires an account, and there's no software to install - it runs in the browser, on desktop or mobile.</p></section>\n\n\n\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s4\"><h2 id=\"s4\" class=\"reveal\">Digital love letter ideas</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A few starting points, if you're staring at a blank page:</p><ul class=\"blog-list reveal delay-1\"><li><strong>Long-distance relationship.</strong> A regular letter, on no particular occasion, is often more meaningful than one tied to an event - it says you were thinking of them on an ordinary day.</li><li><strong>Anniversary.</strong> Pair it with a photo strip from the actual date, or from as close to it as you have.</li><li><strong>Birthday.</strong> A letter reads as more considered than a card, without much more effort.</li><li><strong>Travel memory.</strong> Written while somewhere, or written afterward about somewhere - both work.</li><li><strong>First-date memory.</strong> Revisiting the specifics of how something started tends to land better than a general \"I love you.\"</li><li><strong>A thank-you note.</strong> For something that a text would undersell.</li><li><strong>A letter to a friend.</strong> The format isn't romantic by default - it works just as well for friendship as for a relationship.</li></ul><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">These are starting points, not features of the tool itself - what you write is entirely up to you. The format works whether the occasion is large or nonexistent; a letter written for no particular reason, on an ordinary Tuesday, often reads as more genuine than one written because a date on the calendar required it.</p></section>\n\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s5\"><h2 id=\"s5\" class=\"reveal\">Digital letter vs. sending a normal message</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Neither is objectively better; they do different jobs.</p><div class=\"blog-table-wrap reveal delay-1\"><table class=\"blog-table\"><caption>Digital letter vs. a normal message</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\">Digital letter</th><th scope=\"col\">Normal message</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Time to send</th><td>A few minutes</td><td>Seconds</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Feels like</th><td>An event</td><td>A conversation</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Best for</th><td>Something considered</td><td>Something quick</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Carries photos well</th><td>Yes, built in</td><td>Attached separately</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Reread later</th><td>Feels intentional</td><td>Gets lost in the thread</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A normal message is right for most of a day's communication. A letter is right for the handful of things worth more than a normal message.</p></section>\n<aside class=\"blog-inline-cta reveal\" aria-label=\"Try ConstBooth Letters\"><p class=\"blog-inline-cta-text\">Free, no account needed. Takes a few minutes.</p><a class=\"blog-inline-cta-btn\" href=\"/studio/letters\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:1.1em;height:1.1em;vertical-align:-.15em;margin-right:6px;display:inline-block\"><path d=\"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/></svg>Write a Letter</a></aside>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s6\"><h2 id=\"s6\" class=\"reveal\">If you'd rather record than write</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Not every message wants to be written. If what you're trying to send is your actual voice rather than your handwriting, <a href=\"/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message\" class=\"inline-link\">a digital cassette</a> does the same job with a recording instead of a page - the same idea of something built to be kept, not just read once and forgotten.</p></section>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"faq\"><h2 id=\"faq\" class=\"reveal\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">What is a digital love letter?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A letter written on a realistic digital paper page, with photos, a date and small decorations added, then physically folded and placed into an envelope before it is shared - the digital version keeps the gestures of a real letter rather than replacing them with a form.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">Can I add photos to a digital letter?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Yes. You can add or upload photos or photo strips, then resize and reposition them on the page.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">Can I make a digital letter for a friend?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Yes. It isn't limited to romantic messages - the same format works for friends, family, or anyone a normal message would undersell.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">Can I share a digital love letter online?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Yes, using the supported sharing options once the letter is finished, or you can save it.</p></div></section>\n<div class=\"blog-tag-row\" aria-label=\"Article tags\"><span class=\"blog-tag-label\">Filed under</span><a class=\"blog-tag-chip\" href=\"/blog/tag/long-distance\" rel=\"tag\">Long Distance</a></div><section class=\"blog-related\" aria-labelledby=\"related-heading\"><h2 id=\"related-heading\" class=\"blog-related-title\">Keep reading</h2><div class=\"blog-related-grid\"><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/creative-ways-to-make-digital-memories-online\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Studio</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">3 Creative Ways to Make Digital Memories Online</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">Letters, cassettes and ConstBooth Radio - three formats, and which one fits what you’re after.</span></a><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Studio</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">How to Make a Digital Cassette With Your Voice, Photos &amp; Memories</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">When a recording says more than a page - how to make a digital cassette.</span></a><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/long-distance-relationship-activities\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Long Distance</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">20 Long-Distance Relationship Activities</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">Small, repeatable activities for couples apart, including letters on paper, posted.</span></a><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/why-printed-photos-still-matter\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Culture</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">Why Printed Photos Still Matter</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">The case for things you can hold, in a world of things you only scroll past.</span></a></div></section><div style=\"margin-top:48px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/blog\" class=\"inline-link\" style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:600\">&larr; Back to blog</a></div>\n\n</article></div></div></main><footer class=\"site-footer\"><div class=\"footer-main\"><div class=\"footer-brand\"><div class=\"footer-logo\"><a href=\"/\" aria-label=\"ConstBooth\"><img src=\"/assets/logo-footer.svg?v=b1cb43c4\" alt=\"ConstBooth\" class=\"footer-logo-img\" width=\"134\" height=\"36\"></a></div><p class=\"footer-tagline\">One frame. Beyond distance.</p><div class=\"footer-socials\"><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/app.lensbooth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"footer-social-link\" aria-label=\"Instagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://w